<section>
  <p class="kicker"><%= link_to_page "skyblip-go", label: "skyBlip Go", class: "cta" %></p>
  <h1>Every screen, as the firmware draws it.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Each picture is the 200&times;200 framebuffer of the
    <%= link_to_page "skyblip-go", label: "simulator", anchor: "simulator" %>,
    driven into that state and read out pixel for pixel. A screen that changes
    on the device is a capture taken again.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker" id="both-ways">The radar, both ways</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    <span class="mono">PLOT</span> on the settings menu draws the radar one of
    two ways. <span class="mono">ALL</span>, the first choice and the one a
    device ships on, shrinks the ring and stands every aircraft past it on the
    band around it, on its bearing. <span class="mono">TO SCALE</span> puts
    every mark where the ring&rsquo;s scale puts it, and leaves off what does
    not fit. Three skies, each captured both ways off the same firmware.
  </p>

  <div class="plot" data-controller="plot" data-plot-view-value="both">
    <p class="plot-choices" data-plot-target="choices" hidden>
      <button type="button" class="plot-choice" data-plot-target="choice" data-action="plot#show" data-plot-view-param="all">PLOT ALL</button>
      <button type="button" class="plot-choice" data-plot-target="choice" data-action="plot#show" data-plot-view-param="to-scale">PLOT TO SCALE</button>
      <button type="button" class="plot-choice" data-plot-target="choice" data-action="plot#show" data-plot-view-param="both">Side by side</button>
    </p>

    <div class="plot-situation">
      <h3 id="quiet-sky">A sky that fits the ring.</h3>
      <p>
        Three aircraft inside four miles. With <span class="mono">ALL</span>
        they sit in the smaller ring, and nothing else changes. To scale, the
        ring is the large one.
      </p>
      <div class="shots">
        <figure class="shot plot-all">
          <%= screen_image_tag "radar.png", alt: "The radar page with PLOT ALL: the same three aircraft inside a smaller ring, and nothing on the band around it" %>
          <figcaption>PLOT ALL</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="shot plot-to-scale">
          <%= screen_image_tag "radar-to-scale.png", alt: "The radar page to scale: three aircraft inside the four-mile ring, each with its one-minute leader line" %>
          <figcaption>PLOT TO SCALE</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="plot-situation">
      <h3 id="past-the-ring">Traffic past the ring.</h3>
      <p>
        One aircraft closing from five miles ahead, a gaggle of three eight
        miles off the right of the nose, one eleven miles to the left. With
        <span class="mono">ALL</span>, each stands on the band, the gaggle is
        one mark counted 3, and the closing one&rsquo;s minute is already inside
        the ring. To scale, only the one ahead reaches the glass.
      </p>
      <div class="shots">
        <figure class="shot plot-all">
          <%= screen_image_tag "far-all.png", alt: "The radar page with PLOT ALL: on the band, an aircraft ahead with its leader entering the ring, one mark counted 3 to the upper right, and one aircraft to the left" %>
          <figcaption>PLOT ALL</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="shot plot-to-scale">
          <%= screen_image_tag "far-to-scale.png", alt: "The radar page to scale: the aircraft in the ring, and one more at the very top of the glass; the gaggle and the aircraft to the left are not drawn" %>
          <figcaption>PLOT TO SCALE</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="plot-situation">
      <h3 id="astern">Traffic astern.</h3>
      <p>
        Three aircraft six to eight miles behind, and one inside the ring. With
        <span class="mono">ALL</span> they are one mark counted 3, stepped aside
        from the range label rather than under it. To scale, the three are off
        the glass.
      </p>
      <div class="shots">
        <figure class="shot plot-all">
          <%= screen_image_tag "astern-all.png", alt: "The radar page with PLOT ALL: the same aircraft in the ring, and beside the range label at the bottom one mark counted 3 for the aircraft astern" %>
          <figcaption>PLOT ALL</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="shot plot-to-scale">
          <%= screen_image_tag "astern-to-scale.png", alt: "The radar page to scale: one aircraft in the ring behind and to the left, nothing else" %>
          <figcaption>PLOT TO SCALE</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p><%= link_to_page "radar", label: "How the band reads", anchor: "every-aircraft", class: "cta cta--next" %></p>
</section>

